// Title: Port Forwarding Activity Via SSH.EXE
// Sigma ID: 327f48c1-a6db-4eb8-875a-f6981f1b0183
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-12 | Modified: 2024-03-05
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, lateral-movement, T1572, T1021.001, T1021.004
// Description: Detects port forwarding activity via SSH.exe
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity using a remote port forwarding to a local port
// References:
//   - https://www.absolomb.com/2018-01-26-Windows-Privilege-Escalation-Guide/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ssh_port_forward.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ssh.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -R " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /R " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –R " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —R " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―R ")
